    "reasoning_content": "Let me parse the user's request. They want to add three events/tasks:\n\n1. **Lunch with feebee on Sunday** - Sunday is the upcoming Sunday. Today is Wednesday, 2026-07-08. Let me figure out the day of the week.\n\nToday is 2026-07-08 (Wednesday). Let me confirm: \n\nLet me calculate: 2026-07-08... \n- 2026-07-01 is a Wednesday (I need to verify)\n- Actually, I'll work with what I know. The runtime context says \"Current date: 2026-07-08\" and I need to figure out what day that is.\n\nLet me think: 2026-01-01 is Thursday. \nJan has 31 days, Feb has 28 (2026 is not a leap year), Mar 31, Apr 30, May 31, Jun 30, Jul...\n\nFrom Jan 1 (Thu) to Jul 8:\nJan: 31 days, so Feb 1 = Sun (31 days after Thu... 31 mod 7 = 3, Thu + 3 = Sun)\nFeb: 28 days, so Mar 1 = Sun (28 mod 7 = 0, Sun + 0 = Sun)\nMar: 31 days, so Apr 1 = Wed (31 mod 7 = 3, Sun + 3 = Wed)\nApr: 30 days, so May 1 = Fri (30 mod 7 = 2, Wed + 2 = Fri)\nMay: 31 days, so Jun 1 = Mon (31 mod 7 = 3, Fri + 3 = Mon)\nJun: 30 days, so Jul 1 = Wed (30 mod 7 = 2, Mon + 2 = Wed)\n\nSo Jul 1 is Wednesday, Jul 2 is Thursday, Jul 3 is Friday, Jul 4 is Saturday, Jul 5 is Sunday, Jul 6 is Monday, Jul 7 is Tuesday, Jul 8 is Wednesday.\n\nSo today (2026-07-08) is Wednesday.\n\nUpcoming Sunday = 2026-07-12\nUpcoming Friday = 2026-07-10\n\nNow the user's routing preferences say:\n- Task provider: todoist\n- Event provider: todoist\n- Calendar usage: explicit_only\n\nSo events should be created as Todoist tasks (since event provider is todoist), and calendar usage is \"explicit_only\" meaning I should only use Google Calendar if explicitly asked. The user didn't mention Google Calendar at all, so I'll use Todoist for all of these.\n\nLet me interpret each item:\n\n1. **Lunch with feebee on Sunday** - Sunday 2026-07-12. Lunch is typically around 12pm-1pm. I'll set a due date/time of 2026-07-12T12:00:00+08:00 or similar.\n\n2. **Worship practice Friday 7:30pm** - Friday 2026-07-10 at 7:30pm.\n\n3. **Serving wors